# ============================================================
# CEDAR PRESS - consolidated ignore file
#
# This repository holds TWO trees that were developed separately and
# merged on 2026-09-02:
#   * the product site (Vite + React, server/, src/, tests/)
#   * the data workspace (code/, data/, dist/, review/)
# Both sections are kept whole. Neither tree's rules are safe to prune
# without reading the tree they belong to - the data workspace's rules in
# particular carry deliberate `!` un-ignores for the two spine files that
# ARE tracked, and losing one would start committing 6 GB of tables.
# ============================================================

# ---------------- product site ----------------
node_modules
# The web build's output. NOT `dist/`: the data workspace tracks 295 files
# under that name, and vite empties its output directory before every build,
# so the two cannot share one. See the note in vite.config.js.
dist-site
*.local
.DS_Store

# Playwright
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/

# Cedar dataset pipeline local state
cedar_source_registry/data/
# The entity reconciliation review page is generated by code/128 from the
# tables, and is 270 KB of table rendered as HTML: an output, regenerated on
# demand, not source. It was tracked once and removed 2026-09-05.
web_claude/

# Restricted source material — NEVER commit to this repo.
# github.com/teim-team/cedar-press is PUBLIC. Obtained rosters carry named
# individuals with personal contact details and are held under unconfirmed
# publication rights. They live outside the repo, under
# "Cedar Press/data/restricted/". Referenced by registry rows, never contained
# in them.
cedar_source_registry/source_records/
cedar_source_registry/research/white_earth_*/
*.bak_*

# ---------------- data workspace ----------------
# Cedar Press - what git tracks and what it does not.
#
# THE RULE: git tracks SOURCE. Code, prose, schemas, manifests, contracts,
# and the identity register. Everything that is CONTENT stays out.
#
# Content is versioned by checksum, not by git: run manifests carry input and
# output logical checksums, and retired data is MOVEd to graveyard/ rather than
# deleted, so the history git would provide already exists elsewhere and is
# stronger (it survives a file being rewritten in place). Putting multi-GB
# tables in git would version bytes we already version, and would make the
# repo unusable for the agents that have to clone it.
#
# Content is identified by EXTENSION ANYWHERE, not by directory, because data
# in this project does not stay in data/ - there are 2.5 GB of raw dumps in
# "Federal Spending/", 21 MB of scraped text in code/ancsa_portal/txt/, and
# loose .dta files at the repo root. A directory-based rule misses all three.
# Anything genuinely source-like that happens to carry a data extension is
# re-included by name in the ALLOWLIST at the bottom.

# --- whole trees that are outputs. These are excluded as DIRECTORIES so git
#     never walks them: data/ alone is 38 GB, and an extension-only rule still
#     makes git descend into every folder looking for the files it does track.
#     (Measured: extension-only staged 17,595 files and did not finish.) ---
/data/*
dist/
logs/
# `review/*` and not `review/`, because git cannot re-include anything under
# an excluded DIRECTORY - the negation below would be silently inert.
review/*
# ...except the fixtures. A check whose proof is not in the repository is a
# check nobody can re-run, and this project's standard is that an invariant is
# proven by injecting the violation rather than asserted. They are code, not
# review output.
!review/fixtures_D/
graveyard/

# --- content, by extension, at any depth ---
*.csv
*.tsv
*.dta
*.sav
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.parquet
*.jsonl
*.ndjson
*.bin
*.zip
*.gz
*.7z
*.pdf
*.txt
*.shp
*.dbf
*.shx
*.prj
*.gpkg
*.geojson
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- never-commit noise ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.bak_*
*.part
*.tmp
.venv/
.env
.env.local
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- licensed / restricted material must never enter version control,
#     regardless of extension or of any allowlist entry below ---
data/restricted/
**/restricted/

# =====================================================================
# ALLOWLIST - source-like files that carry a content extension.
# Must come last: in gitignore the LAST matching rule wins.
# Keep this list short. If it grows, the thing being added is probably
# data, and the answer is a checksum in a manifest, not a git blob.
# =====================================================================

# The identity register: the canonical CE-XXXXX-CC assignments. This is the
# one table that IS source - every other table in the project references it,
# and a silent change to it would be undetectable without git history.
# git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded, so the
# path has to be walked back down one level at a time: allow the spine dir,
# re-exclude its contents, then allow the one file.
!/data/spine/
/data/spine/*
!/data/spine/cedar_identity_register.csv
# cedar_handle_history.csv is tracked for the SAME reason as the register and
# is not regenerable: once a handle is retired, its valid_to and its
# change_reason exist nowhere else. An untracked append-only history is a
# history that dies with the working directory, and an old handle that stops
# resolving is exactly the failure review finding F6 is about.
!/data/spine/cedar_handle_history.csv
# RETIRED 2026-09-04 by 1177 - the file moved to graveyard/cicd/ and the rule
# above now un-ignores a path that does not exist. Kept, because the retirement
# is the point: graveyard/cicd/cedar_handle_history.csv is the binding that
# lets any older artifact naming a handle still be read, and 1180 reads it.

# Added 2026-09-04. All four are SOURCE OF TRUTH, small (~690 KB together),
# and none is regenerable from what remains in the repo:
#
#   cedar_retired_neid_crosswalk.csv  the retired NEID -> cedar_uid binding.
#     1177 deleted the `handle` column from the register BEFORE the values
#     were scrubbed from the datasets, which cut the translation vocabulary
#     from 1,555 to 877 while 13,400 customer rows still carried handles. This
#     file is the repair. Untracked, the next clone cannot scrub a NEID at all.
#   cedar_entity_names.csv            the OFFICIAL name per entity with its
#     register, URL and capture date. Rebuildable only by re-fetching three
#     external sources, one of which is a PDF.
#   cedar_entity_types.csv            the 18 entity-class definitions. 1181
#     FAILS the build if a class in the data has no definition here.
#   cedar_nonprofit_ein_links.csv     EIN -> cedar_uid for 380 Native
#     nonprofits. This is identity, not a derived join.
!/data/spine/cedar_retired_neid_crosswalk.csv
!/data/spine/cedar_entity_names.csv
!/data/spine/cedar_entity_types.csv
!/data/spine/cedar_nonprofit_ein_links.csv

# Reports and audit evidence that live in docs/ - small, prose-adjacent,
# and meaningless without the commit they describe.
!docs/**/*.csv
!docs/**/*.txt

# The site's sample files, tracked by rule rather than by `git add -f`. Every
# one is read by the client, the API and the tests, and a sample the importer
# wrote that nobody force-added is a build that passes on the importer's
# machine and fails everywhere else: 2026-09-05, twenty of them, three red
# deploys. `server/tests/test_collection.py` fails if a manifest sample is not
# in the index.
!/public/data/cedar/samples/**/*.csv

# data/cedar/samples.published.json, the measured record of which declared
# samples the repository does NOT hold (scripts/measure-samples.mjs), is read
# by the client, the API and the tests. Like the manifest and the ledger
# beside it, it is force-added once and tracked from then on: `/data/*` above
# ignores the directory itself, so a negation here cannot reach the file.

# Requirements / lockfiles, wherever they turn up.
!requirements*.txt
!constraints*.txt

# Regenerable caches (name says so).
_profile_cache.json
*_cache.json

# The consolidated owner-decision queue is a curated document, not scratch -
# its history shows what was asked and when it was answered.
!review/OWNER_DECISION_QUEUE.md

# Agent worktrees are private scratch, never part of the tree. Committed as a
# gitlink with no .gitmodules entry they become an unusable pseudo-submodule
# and `git submodule status` fails on a fresh checkout.
.claude/worktrees/
# Shape the Research: the service's SQLite ledger, when CEDAR_PRESS_DB points here.
server/var/
